# Risk rules of this repo, read by the merge hook from the default branch only.
# A PR touching a path of a one-way section is `T2 one-way <section>`: no session merges it, the
# owner (`human.name` in the crew) merges it by hand, or approves it where the repo runs an approve
# gate (the merge hook's refusal says which). `[t2]` paths print `T2` and auto-merge after CI.
# A file without any one-way section is valid: the brake is empty on purpose and each merge says so.
# Grammar: `[section]` and `path <glob>` lines (`**`, `*`, `?`, `{a,b}`).
# One-way sections: brake-change, money, destructive-migration, terraform-secrets.
# Two-way `review: high` sections: trust-loosening and brake-review (a security card worker signs
# before the merge), money-path (no card).

[brake-change]
path .weside/crew.json
path .weside/risk-paths
# The review workflows (`claude-code-review.yml`, `codex-code-review.yml`); helpers such as a skip
# gate are named per repo.
path .github/workflows/*-code-review.yml
